# Fashion Recommendation System — Cursor rules

## V1 goal (source: `docs/system-design/v1/v1-hld.md`)

Ship a learning-grade, production-pattern v1: personalized **top-10** recommendations via **Cache → Retrieve → Filter → Rank → Order** (Two-Tower + XGBoost + FAISS + Redis). Unified **FastAPI + Jinja2 + HTMX** on **ECS Fargate**, ingress via **API Gateway HTTP API** (no ALB). Offline: Glue/Step Functions + SageMaker Pipelines. Target ~**$53/mo** active; deploy/destroy with **Terraform**. Explicit demo: cache hit (~15 ms) vs miss (~190 ms) and SQS cache pre-warm.

## Private docs — do not use

Never reference, cite, or read **`docs/my-docs/`** or anything under it. It is personal-only.

## Referece code - Just uses as inspiration when instructed 

When you are instructed to use anything within **`docs/reference-code`**, treat it strictly as a reference implementation. We may take small inspirations from it, but the actual implementation can be significantly different based on our HLD in **`docs/system-design/v1/v1-hld.md`** and any additional instructions provided.

Do not assume the reference code must be followed exactly. Use it only for guidance where relevant, while prioritizing the architecture, requirements, and design decisions defined in the HLD and the given instructions.

If you have any doubts, ambiguities, or conflicts between the reference code, HLD, and instructions, ask follow-up questions before proceeding.

## Authoritative references

| Topic | Document |
|-------|----------|
| Requirements (MUST/SHOULD contract) | `docs/system-design/v1/v1-requirements.md` |
